/p>"},{"id":"4781d3df-f646-4c09-85fb-65e933bd5bb7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"two thirds\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1691007959835,"updateDate":1691007959835}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959835, 1691007959835),
    ($SATQ$4837406c$SATQ$, $SATQ$334db357-0b99-4f13-a766-9dde9a462af3$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">An object travels at a constant speed of <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> centimeters per second. At this speed, what is the time, in seconds, that it would take for the object to travel <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math> centimeters?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the object travels at a constant speed of <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> centimeters per second. The speed of the object can be written as <math alttext="StartFraction 6 centimeters Over 1 second EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>second</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represent the time, in seconds, it would take for the object to travel <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math> centimeters. The value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> can be calculated by solving the equation <math alttext="StartFraction 6 centimeters Over 1 second EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 centimeters Over x seconds EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>second</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, which can be written as <math alttext="six oneths equals StartFraction 24 Over x EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="6 equals StartFraction 24 Over x EndFraction"><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> yields <math alttext="6 x equals 24"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>6</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>24</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals 4"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, it would take the object <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> seconds to travel <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math> centimeters.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"4837406c","external_id":"334db357-0b99-4f13-a766-9dde9a462af3","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"c5b2b684-54a5-4965-9923-d05d5b1e9a14","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">An object travels at a constant speed of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> centimeters per second. At this speed, what is the time, in seconds, that it would take for the object to travel <math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math> centimeters?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["4"],"correct_answer":["4"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the object travels at a constant speed of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> centimeters per second. The speed of the object can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 6 centimeters Over 1 second EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>second</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represent the time, in seconds, it would take for the object to travel <math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math> centimeters. The value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> can be calculated by solving the equation <math alttext=\"StartFraction 6 centimeters Over 1 second EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 centimeters Over x seconds EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>second</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"six oneths equals StartFraction 24 Over x EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"6 equals StartFraction 24 Over x EndFraction\"><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"6 x equals 24\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals 4\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, it would take the object <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> seconds to travel <math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math> centimeters.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357401,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"4837406c","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1730147357401,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"334db357-0b99-4f13-a766-9dde9a462af3","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"c5b2b684-54a5-4965-9923-d05d5b1e9a14","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[],"externalid":"334db357-0b99-4f13-a766-9dde9a462af3","keys":["4"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the object travels at a constant speed of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> centimeters per second. The speed of the object can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 6 centimeters Over 1 second En