<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following is closest to the slope of the line of best fit shown?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"5221e4f5-d4e7-484b-98f8-0bcb5d02d90f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.2\"><mn>0.2</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"aa8c6c28-f130-4649-b5f0-8337afc0c835","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.7\"><mn>0.7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"de94dae3-88a1-4b98-9baf-535ad4cc2865","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1.8\"><mn>1.8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3410a075-065e-4a3f-aed6-5d50e0c5ccc6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2.6\"><mn>2.6</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["de94dae3-88a1-4b98-9baf-535ad4cc2865"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. A line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that passes through points <math alttext="left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext="left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> has a slope of <math alttext="StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. The line of best fit shown passes approximately through the points <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 0.2 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext="left parenthesis 5 comma 9.3 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9.3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. It follows that the slope of this line is approximately <math alttext="StartFraction 9.3 minus 0.2 Over 5 minus 0 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>9.3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="StartFraction 9.1 Over 5 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>9.1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="1.82"><mn>1.82</mn></math>. Therefore, of the given choices, <math alttext="1.8"><mn>1.8</mn></math> is closest to the slope of the line of best fit shown.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This value is closest to the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the line of best fit shown.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"4cc05491","external_id":"89491281-dcad-499e-8fe5-2563d680985f","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"cd9fd868-642c-45c0-bca8-175128a122ab","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given scatterplot, a line of best fit for the data is shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from 0 to 10. The y axis ranges from 0 to 15. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 286.56 275.22 \nL 286.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 260.46 \nL 279.36 260.46 \nL 279.36 10.98 \nL 7.2 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 9.200821 268.02 \nL 271.689179 268.02 \nL 271.689179 7.2 \nL 9.200821 7.2 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_3\">\n    <g id=\"xtick_1\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_2\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_3\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_4\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_5\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick