</math> centimeters is equal to <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> meter. Therefore, <math alttext="2,300"><mn>2,300</mn>
</math> centimeters is equivalent to <math alttext="left parenthesis 2,300 centimeters right parenthesis left parenthesis StartFraction 1 meter Over 100 centimeters EndFraction right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2,300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>meter</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="23"><mn>23</mn>
</math> meters.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. <math alttext="0.043"><mn>0.043</mn>
</math> meters is equivalent to <math alttext="4.3"><mn>4.3</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="2,300"><mn>2,300</mn>
</math>, centimeters.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. <math alttext="2,400"><mn>2,400</mn>
</math> meters is equivalent to <math alttext="240,000"><mn>240,000</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="2,300"><mn>2,300</mn>
</math>, centimeters.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. <math alttext="230,000"><mn>230,000</mn>
</math> meters is equivalent to <math alttext="23,000,000"><mn>23,000,000</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="2,300"><mn>2,300</mn>
</math>, centimeters.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"4e375d1f","external_id":"c11c7138-6922-4b01-8ac3-981d24884e18","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"fe8cc9c5-3096-4d68-860b-9627f7fb47f7","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">How many <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">meters</span> are equivalent to <math alttext=\"2,300\"><mn>2,300</mn>\n</math> centimeters? <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 100 centimeters  equals 1 meter right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>meter</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"5f445867-dc20-4b07-9c33-0af8f2568efe","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.043\"><mn>0.043</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"206b5e12-a7ff-439d-9b7b-eff9c7bd0f7c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"445053a9-6a03-4b53-830d-f533e09fac58","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2,400\"><mn>2,400</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"319596c8-26cc-4b71-8288-ef9c435a1854","content":"<p><math alttext=\"230,000\"><mn>230,000</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["206b5e12-a7ff-439d-9b7b-eff9c7bd0f7c"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math> centimeters is equal to <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> meter. Therefore, <math alttext=\"2,300\"><mn>2,300</mn>\n</math> centimeters is equivalent to <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 2,300 centimeters right parenthesis left parenthesis StartFraction 1 meter Over 100 centimeters EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2,300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mt