mpany is (6.25)(19) = 118.75 years. It follows that the number of years that the employee who left had worked for the company is 134 &ndash; 118.75 = 15.25 years.<p>Choice A is incorrect; this is the change in the mean, which isn&rsquo;t the same as the amount of time worked by the employee who left. Choice B is incorrect and likely results from&nbsp;making the assumption that there were still 20 employees, rather than 19, at the company after the employee left and then subtracting the original mean of 6.7 from that result. Choice C is incorrect and likely&nbsp;results from making the assumption that there were still 20 employees, rather than 19, at the company after the employee left.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959634,"updateDate":1691007959634}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959634, 1691007959634),
