.8 comma 1)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following equations is the most appropriate linear model for the data shown?</p>","externalid":"f1d73552-b37d-4f00-870e-29249c5ffb4b","templateid":"a3f29928-1eff-486c-bd5a-c15ae71bf374","vaultid":"6ff383cd-475f-4cdd-ab18-0f2bab6b5faa","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"81612e4a-216d-4184-bac3-d7bd425bbabf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 0.9 plus 9.4 x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow>\n\t<mn>9.4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fa1cc8a5-5316-4e16-9db0-93afd6098cf4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 0.9 minus 9.4 x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mrow>\n\t<mn>9.4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c11e723a-421d-4694-94a3-2db81b8af864","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 9.4 plus 0.9 x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.4</mn>\n<mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"176c1141-f20b-49df-b705-bb9adbd4bb6b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 9.4 minus 0.9 x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.4</mn>\n<mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1691007959834,"updateDate":1691007959834}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959834, 1691007959834),
    ($SATQ$50b99b2d$SATQ$, $SATQ$964d5413-e030-4000-a612-54941886f548$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Objects R and S each travel at a constant speed. The speed of object R is half the speed of object S. Object R travels a distance of <math alttext="4 x"><mrow>
	<mn>4</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches in<em> </em><math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> seconds. Which expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext="24 x"><mrow>
	<mn>24</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"8e7419e7-c22f-4e1d-b775-44644bb45d76","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8e8427e3-31e3-469c-b3e6-9983a9494862","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5ab0515d-e49b-49a8-9977-564eb6095776","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e6a814cb-de56-467b-a8ed-40777e9fc994","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8e8427e3-31e3-469c-b3e6-9983a9494862"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. It's given that object R travels a distance of <math alttext="4 x"><mrow>
	<mn>4</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches in <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> seconds. This speed can be written as <math alttext="StartFraction 4 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. It's given that the speed of object R is half the speed of object S. It follows that the speed of object S is twice the speed of object R, which is <math alttext="2 left parenthesis StartFraction 4 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction right parenthesis"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 8 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math alttext="n"><mi>n</mi>
</math> represent the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext="24 x"><mrow>
	<mn>24</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches. The value of <math alttext="n"><mi>n</mi>
</math> can be found by solving the equation <math alttext="StartFraction 8 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 x inches Over n seconds EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, which can be written as <math alttext="StartFraction 8 x Over y EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 x Over n EndFraction"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mfrac>
			<mrow>
				<mn>8</mn>
				<mi>x</mi>
			</mrow>
			<mi>y</mi>
		</mfrac>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mfrac>
			<mrow>
				<mn>24</mn>
				<mi>x</mi>
			</mrow>
			<mi>n</mi>
		</mfrac>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="n y"><mrow>
	<mi>n</mi>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="8 x n equals 24 x y"><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext="8 x"><mrow>
	<mn>8</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="n equals 3 y"><mrow>
	<mi>n</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>3</mn>
		<mi>y</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the expression <math alttext="3 y"><mrow>
	<mn>3</mn>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
</math> represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext="24 x"><mrow>
	<mn>24</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it would take object S to travel a distance of <math alttext="24 x"><mrow>
	<mn>24</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches if the speed of object R were twice, not half, the speed of object S.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext="128 x"><mrow>
	<mn>128</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches, not <math alttext="24 x"><mrow>
	<mn>24</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object R, not object S, to travel a distance of <math alttext="24 x"><mrow>
	<mn>24</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> inches.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"50b99b2d","external_id":"964d5413-e030-4000-a612-54941886f548","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"b126173b-5042-45d5-8b28-619c64030045","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>Objects R and S each travel at a constant speed. The speed of object R is half the speed of object S. Object R travels a distance of <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches in<em> </em><math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> seconds. Which expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"8e7419e7-c22f-4e1d-b775-44644bb45d76","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8e8427e3-31e3-469c-b3e6-9983a9494862","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5ab0515d-e49b-49a8-9977-564eb6095776","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e6a814cb-de56-467b-a8ed-40777e9fc994","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["8e8427e3-31e3-469c-b3e6-9983a9494862"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that object R travels a distance of <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches in <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> seconds. This speed can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 4 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. It's given that the speed of object R is half the speed of object S. It follows that the speed of object S is twice the speed of object R, which is <math alttext=\"2 left parenthesis StartFraction 4 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 8 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> represent the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches. The value of <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> can be found by solving the equation <math alttext=\"StartFraction 8 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 x inches Over n seconds EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 8 x Over y EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 x Over n EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"n y\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"8 x n equals 24 x y\"><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"8 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"n equals 3 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the expression <math alttext=\"3 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it would take object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches if the speed of object R were twice, not half, the speed of object S.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"128 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>128</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches, not <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object R, not object S, to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357402,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"50b99b2d","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1730147357402,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"964d5413-e030-4000-a612-54941886f548","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"b126173b-5042-45d5-8b28-619c64030045","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"12 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"8e7419e7-c22f-4e1d-b775-44644bb45d76"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"8e8427e3-31e3-469c-b3e6-9983a9494862"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"5ab0515d-e49b-49a8-9977-564eb6095776"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>","id":"e6a814cb-de56-467b-a8ed-40777e9fc994"}],"externalid":"964d5413-e030-4000-a612-54941886f548","keys":["8e8427e3-31e3-469c-b3e6-9983a9494862"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that object R travels a distance of <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches in <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> seconds. This speed can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 4 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. It's given that the speed of object R is half the speed of object S. It follows that the speed of object S is twice the speed of object R, which is <math alttext=\"2 left parenthesis StartFraction 4 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 8 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> represent the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches. The value of <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> can be found by solving the equation <math alttext=\"StartFraction 8 x inches Over y seconds EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 x inches Over n seconds EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>seconds</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, which can be written as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 8 x Over y EndFraction equals StartFraction 24 x Over n EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"n y\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"8 x n equals 24 x y\"><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"8 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"n equals 3 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the expression <math alttext=\"3 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it would take object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches if the speed of object R were twice, not half, the speed of object S.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"128 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>128</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches, not <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object R, not object S, to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches.</p>","stem":"<p>Objects R and S each travel at a constant speed. The speed of object R is half the speed of object S. Object R travels a distance of <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches in<em> </em><math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> seconds. Which expression represents the time, in seconds, it takes object S to travel a distance of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> inches?</p>","type":"mcq","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1730147357402,"updateDate":1730147357402}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357402, 1730147357402),
