</math> units, how must the length change to maintain this ratio?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"55adc9c2-d4fe-4a4e-ab2f-b712e910ade9","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It must decrease by <math alttext=\"24.5\"><mn>24.5</mn>\n</math> units.</p>"},{"id":"cde07a07-e1c9-4fc9-bd2c-f096d5b926e7","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It must increase by <math alttext=\"24.5\"><mn>24.5</mn>\n</math> units.</p>"},{"id":"10d6e8f4-814c-4bcd-942a-574b958ddf65","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It must decrease by <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> units.</p>"},{"id":"2585bdab-a067-4b85-b64a-58c4c1d2484c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It must increase by <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> units.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["cde07a07-e1c9-4fc9-bd2c-f096d5b926e7"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the ratio of the rectangular region&rsquo;s length to its width is <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>. This can be written as a proportion: <math alttext="StartFraction length Over width EndFraction equals StartFraction 35 Over 10 EndFraction"><mfrac><mtext>length</mtext><mtext>width</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="StartFraction script l Over w EndFraction equals StartFraction 35 Over 10 EndFraction"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>. This proportion can be rewritten as <math alttext="10 script l equals 35 w"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mi>w</mi></math>, or <math alttext="script l equals 3.5 w"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.5</mn><mi>w</mi></math>. If the width of the rectangular region increases by <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math>, then the length will increase by some number <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> in order to maintain this ratio. The value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> can be found by replacing&nbsp;<math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> with&nbsp;<math alttext="script l plus x"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></math> and <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> with <math alttext="w plus 7"><mrow>
	<mi>w</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>7</mn>
</mrow>
</math> in the equation, which gives <math alttext="script l plus x equals 3.5 left parenthesis w plus 7 right parenthesis"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. This equation can be rewritten using the distributive property as <math alttext="script l plus x equals 3.5 w plus 24.5"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.5</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>24.5</mn></math>. Since&nbsp;<math alttext="script l equals 3.5 w"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.5</mn><mi>w</mi></math>, the right-hand side of this equation can be rewritten by substituting&nbsp;<math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> for <math alttext="3.5 w"><mrow>
	<mn>3.5</mn>
	<mi>w</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, which gives <math alttext="script l plus x equals script l plus 24.5"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>24.5</mn></math>, or <math alttext="x equals 24.5"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>24.5</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, if the width of the rectangular region increases by <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> units, the length must increase by <math alttext="24.5"><mn>24.5</mn>
</math> units in order to maintain the given ratio.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. If the width of the rectangular region increases, the length must also increase, not decrease.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. If the width of the rectangular region increases, the length must also increase, not decrease.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. Since the ratio of the length to the width of the rectangular region is <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>, if the width of the rectangular region increases by <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> units, the length would have to increase by a proportional amount, which would have to be greater than <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> units.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"51c9d65f","external_id":"252ab91d-897c-4c0d-8d50-e60456359300","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"87e2da87-dcba-443c-9ac7-660c022dffd8","uId":"f446937b-00fb-4f60-8d0e-e89e628a1907","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For a certain rectangular region, the ratio of its length to its width is <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math>. If the width of the rectangular region increases by <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> units, how must the length change to maintain this ratio?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"55adc9c2-d4fe-4a4e-ab2f-b712e910ade9","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It must decrease by <math alttext=\"24.5\"><mn>24.5</mn>\n</math> units.</p>"},{"id":"cde07a07-e1c9-4fc9-bd2c-f096d5b926e7","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It must increase by <math alttext=\"24.5\"><mn>24.5</mn>\n</math> units.</p>"},{"id":"10d6e8f4-814c-4bcd-942a-574b958ddf65","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It must decrease by <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> units.</p>"},{"id":"2585bdab-a067-4b85-b64a-58c4c1d2484c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">It must increase by <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> units.</p>"}],"keys":["cde07a07-e1c9-4fc9-bd2c-f096d5b926e7"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the ratio of the rectangular region&rsquo;s length to its width is <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math>. This can be written as a proportion: <math alttext=\"StartFract