    ($SATQ$5267c3c7$SATQ$, $SATQ$fb4b074b-8096-42a7-9ab5-1672ab4556c2$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The result of increasing the quantity <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="400 percent sign"><mn>400</mn>
<mo>%</mo></math> is <math alttext="60"><mn>60</mn>
</math>. What is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"703e7066-896c-4831-8bc0-3b7bee965711","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"20edfab2-8d07-4e5f-a705-cb51b699346c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"88aff368-73b3-4452-aadb-f8b5657b2b83","content":"<p><math alttext=\"240\"><mn>240</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"dac44697-4dfb-4a1b-9b6f-aa3af765af5a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"340\"><mn>340</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["703e7066-896c-4831-8bc0-3b7bee965711"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It's given that the result of increasing the quantity <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="400 percent sign"><mn>400</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is <math alttext="60"><mn>60</mn>
</math>. This can be written as <math alttext="x plus left parenthesis StartFraction 400 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis x equals 60"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>400</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="x plus 4 x equals 60"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>, or <math alttext="5 x equals 60"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>5</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>60</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals 12"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>12</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="12"><mn>12</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The result of increasing the quantity <math alttext="15"><mn>15</mn>
</math> by <math alttext="400 percent sign"><mn>400</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext="75"><mn>75</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="60"><mn>60</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. The result of increasing the quantity <math alttext="240"><mn>240</mn>
</math> by <math alttext="400 percent sign"><mn>400</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext="1,200"><mn>1,200</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="60"><mn>60</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. The result of increasing the quantity <math alttext="340"><mn>340</mn>
</math> by <math alttext="400 percent sign"><mn>400</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext="1,700"><mn>1,700</mn>
